        <h1>Business Requirements Document</h1>
    <h1>Business Requirements Document (BRD)</h1><p>Document Version: 1.0
Date: 2026-02-20
Prepared By: Business Analysis Team</p><h2>1. Executive Summary</h2><p>The purpose of this Business Requirements Document is to outline the functional and non-functional requirements for implementing a next-generation Customer Relationship Management (CRM) system. This system will support key business processes across sales, marketing, and customer support.

The project aims to accelerate customer onboarding, improve lead conversion rates, and provide actionable insights through KPI dashboards and machine learning predictions.</p><h2>2. Business Objectives</h2><ul><li>Increase customer retention by 20% within the first 12 months.</li><li>Reduce lead conversion processing time by 30%.</li><li>Create a centralized customer data repository.</li><li>Improve reporting capabilities for strategic decision-making.</li></ul><h2>3. Stakeholders</h2><p>The following stakeholders have a vested interest in the success of this project:</p><ul><li>Chief Executive Officer (CEO)</li><li>Chief Operating Officer (COO)</li><li>Sales Director</li><li>Marketing Manager</li><li>IT Director</li><li>Customer Support Team Lead</li></ul><h2>4. Scope</h2><p>The scope details what is included and excluded in this CRM implementation project.</p><h3>4.1 In-Scope</h3><ul><li>User management and authentication</li><li>Lead tracking and qualification system</li><li>Customer service ticketing module</li><li>Reporting dashboards for sales and marketing</li></ul><h3>4.2 Out-of-Scope</h3><ul><li>Mobile native application</li><li>Billing and invoicing module</li><li>Third-party integrations not specified separately</li></ul><h2>5. Functional Requirements</h2><table><tr><th>Req ID</th><th>Description</th><th>Priority</th><th>Source</th></tr><tr><td>FR-001</td><td>User login with multi-factor authentication</td><td>High</td><td>Security Policy</td></tr><tr><td>FR-002</td><td>Role-based access control</td><td>High</td><td>Stakeholder Workshop</td></tr><tr><td>FR-003</td><td>Customer 360 profile page</td><td>Medium</td><td>Business Case</td></tr><tr><td>FR-004</td><td>Customizable report dashboard</td><td>Medium</td><td>Sales Team</td></tr><tr><td>FR-005</td><td>Automatic lead scoring</td><td>High</td><td>Marketing Requirements</td></tr></table><h2>6. Non-Functional Requirements</h2><p>Non-functional requirements focus on the qualities and constraints of the CRM solution.</p><ul><li>The system must have 99.9% availability.</li><li>Page load time must be under 2 seconds for all screens.</li><li>All data must be encrypted in transit and at rest.</li><li>The system shall support at least 10,000 concurrent users.</li></ul><h2>7. Assumptions and Constraints</h2><ul><li>Assumption: Key business users will be available for requirement reviews.</li><li>Assumption: Network infrastructure will support cloud deployment.</li><li>Constraint: Budget capped at defined project allocation.</li><li>Constraint: Delivery must be completed by Q4 2026.</li></ul><h2>8. Acceptance Criteria</h2><p>The criteria below must be satisfied before the project is considered complete:</p><ol><li>The system must pass all functional test cases with zero critical defects.</li><li>User documentation and training materials must be delivered.</li><li>Stakeholder sign-offs obtained on key modules.</li><li>UAT must be completed and approved by business representatives.</li></ol><h2>9. Glossary</h2><table><tr><th>Term</th><th>Definition</th></tr><tr><td>CRM</td><td>Customer Relationship Management</td></tr><tr><td>UAT</td><td>User Acceptance Testing</td></tr><tr><td>ROI</td><td>Return on Investment</td></tr><tr><td>API</td><td>Application Programming Interface</td></tr></table><h2>10. Appendix</h2><p>Additional reference documents and artifacts related to the CRM project can be found in the project repository. These include architecture diagrams, detailed workflows, and compliance certificates.</p>
